{"step_index":1052,"source":"SYSTEM_SDK","type":"EPHEMERAL_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:48:28Z","content":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nNothing open yet.\n\n# claude-mem status\n\nThis project has no memory yet. The current session will seed it; subsequent sessions will receive auto-injected context for relevant past work.\n\nMemory injection starts on your second session in a project.\n\n`/learn-codebase` is available if the user wants to front-load the entire repo into memory in a single pass (~5 minutes on a typical repo, optional). Otherwise memory builds passively as work happens.\n\nLive activity: http://localhost:37701\n✨ 30 Day Free Trial — memory runs off-plan. Get up to 100% more usage from your plan https://cmem.ai/pro?from=welcome-hint\nHow it works: `/how-it-works`\n\nThis message disappears once the first observation lands.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Search first with mem_search({query, mode: \"auto\", project}) to avoid duplicate or conflicting notes. For guided research, use mode: \"guided\" and follow each returned continuation through mem-search steps 1, 2, and 3. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: call mem_search directly when its result is needed."}
{"step_index":1053,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:48:28Z","input_tokens":8614,"cache_read_tokens":148886,"output_tokens":3129,"thinking":"Focusing on the `HermesDeskPanel.tsx` component, the interface requires a top banner labeled \"Neural Evolution Cockpit.\" This banner will include a level and title badge displaying \"LEVEL 4 • ADAPTIVE QUANT REGIME SPECIALIST,\" and an XP progress bar showing \"XP: 820 / 1,100.\"  Four adaptive weight chips are also needed to display performance metrics, specifically \"Regime Precision: +14.2%,\" \"False Breakout Filter: +18.6%,\" \"Sentiment Calibration: +9.4%,\" and \"Dynamic Sizing Edge: +12.\"\n\n\nThe system's architecture requires a consolidated view of agent data and pending trade approvals. The `HermesDeskPanel` provides this central hub, incorporating a header to communicate operational state and performance. It will also include a detailed order approval modal to allow for explicit trade decisions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import React from 'react';\nimport { PendingOrder } from '../types';\nimport { ShieldAlert, CheckCircle2, XCircle, ArrowUpRight, ArrowDownRight, Clock, Target, AlertTriangle, Sparkles } from 'lucide-react';\n\ninterface OrderApprovalModalProps {\n  order: PendingOrder;\n  onApprove: () => void;\n  onVeto: () => void;\n}\n\nexport const OrderApprovalModal: React.FC<OrderApprovalModalProps> = ({\n  order,\n  onApprove,\n  onVeto\n}) => {\n  const isBuy = order.action === 'BUY';\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center p-4 bg-black/80 backdrop-blur-md animate-in fade-in duration-200\">\n      <div className=\"relative w-full max-w-xl p-6 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-b from-[#11162b] to-[#0c0f1d] border-2 border-indigo-500/50 shadow-[0_0_50px_rgba(99,102,241,0.35)] overflow-hidden\">\n        {/* Glow Effects */}\n        <div className=\"absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-3/4 h-2 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-cyan-400 to-transparent\" />\n        <div className=\"absolute -top-24 -right-24 w-48 h-48 bg-indigo-500/20 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none\" />\n        <div className=\"absolute -bottom-24 -left-24 w-48 h-48 bg-cyan-500/20 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none\" />\n\n        {/* Header */}\n        <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between pb-4 border-b border-slate-800\">\n          <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n            <div className=\"w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-tr from-indigo-600 to-cyan-500 flex items-center justify-center shadow-lg shadow-indigo-500/30\">\n              <Sparkles className=\"w-5 h-5 text-white animate-pulse\" />\n            </div>\n            <div>\n              <div className=\"flex items-center gap-2\">\n                <h3 className=\"font-display font-bold text-lg text-white tracking-wide\">\n                  HERMES 7-AGENT DISPATCH\n                </h3>\n                <span className=\"px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-[10px] font-mono font-bold bg-indigo-500/20 text-indigo-300 border border-indigo-500/40\">\n                  HITL APPROVAL\n                </span>\n              </div>\n              <p className=\"text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono\">\n                Operator confirmation required before broker routing\n              </p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div className=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/30 text-amber-300 font-mono text-xs\">\n            <Clock className=\"w-3.5 h-3.5 animate-spin\" />\n            <span>Standing by</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Order Details Grid */}\n        <div className=\"my-5 p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/80 border border-slate-800/80 space-y-4\">\n          {/* Main Pair & Action */}\n          <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between\">\n            <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n              <span className=\"text-2xl font-mono font-black text-white tracking-tight\">\n                {order.instrument}\n              </span>\n              <span className={`px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg font-mono font-black text-xs flex items-center gap-1 ${\n                isBuy\n                  ? 'bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-500/40'\n                  : 'bg-rose-500/20 text-rose-300 border border-rose-500/40'\n              }`}>\n                {isBuy ? <ArrowUpRight className=\"w-3.5 h-3.5\" /> : <ArrowDownRight className=\"w-3.5 h-3.5\" />}\n                {order.action} ORDER\n              </span>\n            </div>\n\n            <div className=\"text-right\">\n              <div className=\"text-[10px] font-mono uppercase text-slate-400\">Hydra Quality</div>\n              <span className=\"text-xs font-mono font-bold text-cyan-300 bg-cyan-500/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-cyan-500/30\">\n                Grade {order.setupGrade} ({order.gradeScore}/100)\n              </span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          {/* Pricing Levels */}\n          <div className=\"grid grid-cols-3 gap-2.5 pt-2 border-t border-slate-800/80\">\n            <div className=\"p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-800/40 border border-slate-700/40\">\n              <div className=\"text-[10px] font-mono uppercase text-slate-400\">Entry Target</div>\n              <div className=\"text-sm font-mono font-bold text-white mt-0.5\">\n                ${order.entryPrice.toLocaleString()}\n              </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div className=\"p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-rose-950/20 border border-rose-500/30\">\n              <div className=\"text-[10px] font-mono uppercase text-rose-400 flex items-center gap-1\">\n                <ShieldAlert className=\"w-3 h-3\" /> Stop Loss\n              </div>\n              <div className=\"text-sm font-mono font-bold text-rose-300 mt-0.5\">\n                ${order.stopLoss.toLocaleString()}\n              </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div className=\"p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-emerald-950/20 border border-emerald-500/30\">\n              <div className=\"text-[10px] font-mono uppercase text-emerald-400 flex items-center gap-1\">\n                <Target className=\"w-3 h-3\" /> Profit Target\n              </div>\n              <div className=\"text-sm font-mono font-bold text-emerald-300 mt-0.5\">\n                ${order.targetPrice.toLocaleString()}\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          {/* Sentinel Risk Rule */}\n          <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-indigo-950/30 border border-indigo-500/30 text-xs font-mono\">\n            <div className=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-indigo-300\">\n              <AlertTriangle className=\"w-4 h-4 text-amber-400\" />\n              <span>Sentinel Cap: Strict 0.75% Max Risk</span>\n            </div>\n            <div className=\"font-bold text-white\">\n              Risk: ${order.riskUsd.toFixed(2)} <span className=\"text-emerald-400\">(Reward: +${order.potentialProfitUsd.toFixed(2)})</span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          {/* AI Committee Synthesis */}\n          <div className=\"p-3 rounded-lg bg-slate-950/60 border border-slate-800 text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-sans\">\n            <span className=\"font-mono font-bold text-indigo-400\">Hermes Rationale: </span>\n            {order.rationale}. Atlas confirms trend direction; Lumen reports clear macro news window.\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        {/* Action Buttons */}\n        <div className=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 pt-2\">\n          <button\n            onClick={onVeto}\n            className=\"flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-800/80 hover:bg-rose-950/40 text-slate-300 hover:text-rose-300 font-display font-semibold text-sm border border-slate-700/80 hover:border-rose-500/50 transition-all duration-200 active:scale-95\"\n          >\n            <XCircle className=\"w-4 h-4 text-rose-400\" />\n            Veto / Stand Aside (+15 XP)\n          </button>\n\n          <button\n            onClick={onApprove}\n            className=\"flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 via-teal-600 to-emerald-500 hover:from-emerald-500 hover:to-teal-400 text-white font-display font-bold text-sm shadow-lg shadow-emerald-600/30 border border-emerald-400/40 transition-all duration-200 active:scale-95 hover:shadow-emerald-500/50\"\n          >\n            <CheckCircle2 className=\"w-4 h-4 text-white\" />\n            Approve Order (+35 XP)\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n","Description":"Create OrderApprovalModal.tsx for Human-In-The-Loop execution with risk metrics and XP incentives","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/Users/dev/Documents/Antigravity/grok-bot-dashboard/src/components/OrderApprovalModal.tsx","toolAction":"Creating OrderApprovalModal.tsx","toolSummary":"Create OrderApprovalModal"}}]}
